00:59:57.193 --> 01:00:00.863
Especially since I think in my life

01:00:02.565 --> 01:00:03.633
Work is work

01:00:03.633 --> 01:00:06.102
When I'm relaxing, I just find different work to do

01:00:06.369 --> 01:00:07.103
So for me

01:00:07.103 --> 01:00:09.038
My best companions are Claude and Gemini

01:00:10.039 --> 01:00:13.910
But it might not be like that for others

01:00:13.910 --> 01:00:15.712
So it might just be my personal thing

01:00:15.979 --> 01:00:18.181
The one or two times I used Doubao myself

01:00:18.948 --> 01:00:21.250
It was because someone showed me the Doubao phone

01:00:21.351 --> 01:00:22.952
Hahahaha, right

01:00:23.152 --> 01:00:24.187
So what do you think of the Doubao phone?

01:00:25.421 --> 01:00:29.926
I think it's a great idea

01:00:29.926 --> 01:00:31.361
Personally, in terms of results

01:00:31.361 --> 01:00:33.296
They actually did a pretty good job

01:00:33.763 --> 01:00:36.132
Of course, what I don't know is

01:00:36.432 --> 01:00:39.302
Technically, how well optimized it is

01:00:39.302 --> 01:00:39.969
I mean, it

01:00:39.969 --> 01:00:43.139
I think it executes some tasks in real time

01:00:43.139 --> 01:00:44.741
From a results perspective, there's no problem

01:00:44.774 --> 01:00:47.477
But I don't know how much overhead it has

01:00:47.944 --> 01:00:49.545
If that overhead is very, very large

01:00:49.646 --> 01:00:51.848
Then it's probably a technical issue that needs to be solved. Mm-hmm.

01:00:51.848 --> 01:00:53.983
Because you don't want, you know

01:00:53.983 --> 01:00:56.986
Your model to book a high-speed train ticket for you

01:00:57.120 --> 01:00:59.188
And end up costing more than the ticket itself

01:00:59.655 --> 01:01:01.257
That would definitely be unacceptable

01:01:02.258 --> 01:01:03.693
Right, so

01:01:03.693 --> 01:01:05.161
Technically speaking

01:01:05.161 --> 01:01:08.097
I personally don't know how mature it is

01:01:08.364 --> 01:01:10.366
And from a product perspective

01:01:10.666 --> 01:01:12.201
For everyone, it's still quite

01:01:12.201 --> 01:01:12.869
Can't say surprising

01:01:12.869 --> 01:01:14.437
But it's something that gets people pretty excited

01:01:14.637 --> 01:01:15.038
And I think

01:01:15.038 --> 01:01:17.640
Apple probably wanted to do something like this before

01:01:17.974 --> 01:01:20.076
It's just that Apple's own models haven't been that great

01:01:20.276 --> 01:01:21.778
