01:29:18.619 --> 01:29:19.754
Eh, quantum physics

01:29:19.754 --> 01:29:21.456
What kind of worldview is it as a whole

01:29:21.889 --> 01:29:23.157
It and, um

01:29:23.591 --> 01:29:24.092
I think

01:29:24.092 --> 01:29:26.928
I think the biggest difference is I think, um

01:29:27.428 --> 01:29:27.862
There are many

01:29:27.862 --> 01:29:30.264
Many differences from classical physics

01:29:30.264 --> 01:29:30.965
But I think

01:29:30.965 --> 01:29:32.266
They are two corresponding concepts, right

01:29:32.266 --> 01:29:33.301
Classical physics and quantum physics

01:29:34.502 --> 01:29:38.840
They are theories at different energy and time

01:29:38.840 --> 01:29:40.041
Or spatial scales

01:29:40.041 --> 01:29:43.244
That is, essentially our world is all quantum

01:29:43.244 --> 01:29:44.078
Of course right now

01:29:44.078 --> 01:29:45.880
We don't know what exists at smaller scales

01:29:45.880 --> 01:29:46.647
Right, like
At smaller scales

01:29:46.647 --> 01:29:49.183
There are many different ideas

01:29:49.183 --> 01:29:50.451
For example, string theory is an idea

01:29:50.451 --> 01:29:52.353
And then look at other ideas

01:29:52.353 --> 01:29:53.488
Quantum gravity is also an idea, things like that

01:29:53.955 --> 01:29:55.289
Right, but none of those can be verified

01:29:55.289 --> 01:29:56.290
Verified

01:29:56.657 --> 01:29:59.360
The effective theory at the smallest scales is quantum physics

01:29:59.594 --> 01:30:01.429
The tiniest, tiniest scales

01:30:01.729 --> 01:30:04.132
That can be experimentally verified

01:30:04.599 --> 01:30:07.835
The effective theory at the smallest scales is quantum

01:30:07.835 --> 01:30:10.171
Of course, this includes quantum mechanics and quantum field theory

01:30:10.638 --> 01:30:12.140
And classical physics is

01:30:12.140 --> 01:30:16.177
When the spatial scale you're looking at and

01:30:16.177 --> 01:30:17.645
Is relatively large

01:30:17.945 --> 01:30:18.513
This quantum physics

01:30:18.513 --> 01:30:20.114
Will gradually, gradually reduce to classical physics

01:30:20.715 --> 01:30:23.117
Actually, it's more about at different scales

01:30:23.117 --> 01:30:24.452
Having different effective theories

01:30:24.752 --> 01:30:26.187
This, this thing

01:30:26.187 --> 01:30:28.623
Is actually a very profound idea in physics

01:30:28.623 --> 01:30:29.791
It's what's called the renormalization group

01:30:29.791 --> 01:30:31.659
What the renormalization group says

01:30:31.659 --> 01:30:33.361
Is that

01:30:34.262 --> 01:30:37.799
The theory describing a system

01:30:37.965 --> 01:30:39.333
At different energy scales

01:30:39.333 --> 01:30:41.002
May look completely different

01:30:41.969 --> 01:30:45.206
Right, and even if they may ultimately, at the root

01:30:45.206 --> 01:30:46.808
Are all a grand unified theory

01:30:46.808 --> 01:30:47.408
Of course, right now

01:30:47.408 --> 01:30:49.143
There isn't really a true grand unified theory

01:30:49.343 --> 01:30:50.311
If one exists

01:30:50.311 --> 01:30:52.346
Even if they share the same root at the origin

01:30:52.513 --> 01:30:53.448
But at different scales

01:30:53.448 --> 01:30:55.249
They may also look completely different

01:30:55.750 --> 01:30:57.452
So classical physics and

01:30:57.452 --> 01:30:57.852
Quantum physics

01:30:57.852 --> 01:30:59.687
Are more like two descriptions at different scales

01:31:00.488 --> 01:31:01.189
Speaking of quantum physics

01:31:01.189 --> 01:31:03.257
There are several terms that seem related

01:31:03.291 --> 01:31:04.559
For example, the butterfly effect

01:31:05.059 --> 01:31:06.494
For example, quantum entanglement

01:31:06.994 --> 01:31:08.329
Can you talk about these

01:31:08.763 --> 01:31:10.264
I think this is something everyone can understand

01:31:10.264 --> 01:31:11.165
And I don't know physics either

01:31:11.165 --> 01:31:12.133
Don't blame me, everyone

01:31:12.333 --> 01:31:13.634
I don't know quantum physics either

01:31:14.569 --> 01:31:15.636
Right, I think

01:31:15.636 --> 01:31:16.737
Quantum entanglement

01:31:16.737 --> 01:31:19.674
Is indeed something relatively well-known

01:31:19.674 --> 01:31:22.009
And quite unique to quantum physics

01:31:22.176 --> 01:31:23.377
And then it's very simple

01:31:23.377 --> 01:31:24.879
It's like, say I have two particles

01:31:24.879 --> 01:31:26.147
For example, they're in an entangled state

01:31:26.147 --> 01:31:29.550
And then maybe they're actually very far apart

01:31:29.550 --> 01:31:29.984
But actually

01:31:29.984 --> 01:31:31.786
If I perform some measurement on one of them

01:31:31.786 --> 01:31:32.553
Or perturbation

01:31:32.553 --> 01:31:34.322
It will also affect the state of the other

01:31:34.655 --> 01:31:35.690
This is real

01:31:35.756 --> 01:31:36.724
This is real, right

01:31:37.325 --> 01:31:39.327
What kinds of things have quantum entanglement

01:31:39.760 --> 01:31:41.062
What kinds of two objects, there are many

01:31:41.062 --> 01:31:42.930
There are many

01:31:43.064 --> 01:31:44.565
Just, there are many

01:31:44.565 --> 01:31:45.166
Actual situations

01:31:45.166 --> 01:31:46.100
It's actually

01:31:46.100 --> 01:31:49.136
When you look closely enough, enough, enough

01:31:49.136 --> 01:31:50.571
At a small enough, microscopic scale

01:31:50.571 --> 01:31:53.574
The vast majority of particles may be in entangled states

01:31:54.008 --> 01:31:55.109
But practically speaking

01:31:55.109 --> 01:31:58.246
You can
For example, create one spin and another spin

01:31:58.246 --> 01:31:59.747
First bring them together

01:31:59.747 --> 01:32:02.683
Then collapse them into an entangled state

01:32:02.717 --> 01:32:04.685
Then you can pull one of them very far away

01:32:04.785 --> 01:32:06.287
Then it becomes an entanglement

01:32:06.320 --> 01:32:07.321
A state entangled over a long distance

01:32:07.922 --> 01:32:10.992
And I think even, I remember a few years ago

01:32:10.992 --> 01:32:13.060
There were people who specifically did experiments

01:32:13.427 --> 01:32:15.596
Putting a bacterium and some other thing

01:32:15.596 --> 01:32:17.498
Into a quantum entangled state

01:32:17.932 --> 01:32:19.333
What do you mean by prepare

01:32:19.333 --> 01:32:22.270
Into a quantum entangled state

01:32:22.270 --> 01:32:23.638
This can be manually operated

01:32:23.638 --> 01:32:24.972
This is something that can be manually operated

01:32:25.106 --> 01:32:26.507
Why, how do you operate it

01:32:26.607 --> 01:32:27.975
Generally speaking

01:32:27.975 --> 01:32:29.710
It's through some

01:32:29.710 --> 01:32:32.079
Some measurements and the action of evolution operators

01:32:32.079 --> 01:32:32.580
Can put it

01:32:32.580 --> 01:32:33.648
Into this state

01:32:34.081 --> 01:32:35.650
But the hard part here

01:32:35.650 --> 01:32:37.618
Is actually how to implement this experimentally

01:32:37.618 --> 01:32:38.286
This process

01:32:38.552 --> 01:32:39.287
You can imagine

01:32:39.287 --> 01:32:41.389
It's like you perform some quantum measurements

01:32:41.389 --> 01:32:43.991
And some, some so-called quantum gate operations

01:32:43.991 --> 01:32:45.760
Actually

01:32:45.760 --> 01:32:46.494
It's quite difficult

01:32:46.494 --> 01:32:49.397
Which brings us back to the question just now

01:32:49.397 --> 01:32:51.299
That every system is actually not isolated

01:32:51.432 --> 01:32:52.967
You might have these two spins

01:32:52.967 --> 01:32:53.367
And you think, hey

01:32:53.367 --> 01:32:54.001
If I prepare them this way

01:32:54.001 --> 01:32:55.836
Don't I get an entangled state?

01:32:55.836 --> 01:32:57.438
Then I just separate them and I'm done

01:32:57.438 --> 01:32:58.573
But the real problem is

01:32:58.573 --> 01:33:00.741
These two particles actually live in our world

01:33:01.008 --> 01:33:01.876
Other particles constantly

01:33:01.876 --> 01:33:02.743
Bump into them

01:33:02.777 --> 01:33:04.612
Or external heat disturbs them a bit

01:33:04.612 --> 01:33:05.746
And the state is gone just like that

01:33:05.880 --> 01:33:06.414
So the hard part is

01:33:06.414 --> 01:33:08.783
How to actually implement this process experimentally

01:33:08.950 --> 01:33:10.818
Right, and then

01:33:10.818 --> 01:33:13.354
Another example of entanglement might be more well-known

01:33:13.354 --> 01:33:14.889
I should actually mention that example

01:33:14.889 --> 01:33:16.657
Which is Schrödinger's cat

01:33:16.657 --> 01:33:17.625
Schrödinger's cat

01:33:17.625 --> 01:33:21.462
That's a much more famous example

01:33:21.462 --> 01:33:24.098
It says its state is actually a superposition

01:33:24.098 --> 01:33:26.801
Of a radioactive source emitting a particle

01:33:26.801 --> 01:33:28.302
And the cat being dead

01:33:28.769 --> 01:33:29.604
That's one state

01:33:29.971 --> 01:33:31.806
The other state is the radioactive source not emitting a particle

01:33:31.806 --> 01:33:33.908
And the cat being alive, a superposition of these two

01:33:34.041 --> 01:33:34.508
So for example

01:33:34.508 --> 01:33:36.310
If you measure that radioactive source

01:33:36.310 --> 01:33:37.912
And find that it emitted a particle

01:33:37.912 --> 01:33:38.813
You know the cat is dead

01:33:39.447 --> 01:33:41.716
No matter how far apart the cat and the source are

01:33:42.149 --> 01:33:44.518
Right, so that's entanglement

01:33:44.518 --> 01:33:47.622
But the butterfly effect is a

01:33:48.222 --> 01:33:49.523
Is a different thing

01:33:49.523 --> 01:33:50.858
And the butterfly effect

01:33:52.126 --> 01:33:54.528
Well the famous part of the butterfly effect

01:33:54.528 --> 01:33:55.930
Is actually from classical physics

01:33:56.297 --> 01:33:58.466
What people hear about in classical physics

01:33:58.466 --> 01:34:01.068
The butterfly effect is that famous example

01:34:01.068 --> 01:34:02.303
Where maybe a butterfly in South America

01:34:02.303 --> 01:34:03.637
Flaps its wings

01:34:03.838 --> 01:34:04.538
Half a month later

01:34:04.538 --> 01:34:06.407
A typhoon hits North America

01:34:07.441 --> 01:34:10.911
But from a more mathematical formulation

01:34:10.911 --> 01:34:14.315
It says that at time

01:34:15.850 --> 01:34:16.751
At the initial moment

01:34:16.751 --> 01:34:19.020
If you make a very tiny perturbation

01:34:19.420 --> 01:34:21.355
And then measure the impact of this perturbation

01:34:21.355 --> 01:34:22.690
How large it becomes in the future

01:34:22.723 --> 01:34:23.224
You'll find

01:34:23.224 --> 01:34:26.661
That this perturbation grows exponentially

01:34:27.161 --> 01:34:28.429
Right, that's mathematically

01:34:28.429 --> 01:34:30.731
A description of the classical butterfly effect

01:34:31.332 --> 01:34:34.668
But something people were puzzled about before

01:34:35.136 --> 01:34:37.471
Is how could this phenomenon exist in quantum systems

01:34:37.805 --> 01:34:39.140
Because as we just said, isolated

01:34:39.140 --> 01:34:40.408
An isolated quantum system undergoes unitary evolution

01:34:40.408 --> 01:34:41.809
It's a very linear process

01:34:42.043 --> 01:34:44.245
So in a certain sense

01:34:44.245 --> 01:34:46.881
If you have one state

01:34:46.881 --> 01:34:48.649
That is, one vector and another vector

01:34:48.649 --> 01:34:50.451
With not too large an angle between them initially

01:34:50.851 --> 01:34:51.952
Then after some evolution

01:34:51.952 --> 01:34:53.454
This angle shouldn't change

01:34:54.055 --> 01:34:56.323
And so there should always exist

01:34:56.323 --> 01:34:58.826
This situation where initial states are

01:34:58.859 --> 01:34:59.627
Very slightly different

01:34:59.627 --> 01:35:01.996
And in the future, bam, it grows exponentially

01:35:02.229 --> 01:35:03.831
That seems from quantum mechanics, like

01:35:03.831 --> 01:35:05.433
Something unlikely to happen

01:35:05.699 --> 01:35:06.333
But as we just said

01:35:06.333 --> 01:35:09.070
Our world is actually quantum at the microscopic level

01:35:09.070 --> 01:35:10.838
And becomes classical at the macroscopic level

01:35:11.072 --> 01:35:12.306
But they're part of the same continuum

01:35:12.306 --> 01:35:13.908
How can one have it and not the other

01:35:13.908 --> 01:35:15.476
That's what people were trying to understand

01:35:15.543 --> 01:35:17.311
And of course
Later people gained a better understanding

01:35:17.311 --> 01:35:19.213
Which is that actually

01:35:19.280 --> 01:35:21.882
When discussing the butterfly effect in quantum systems

01:35:21.882 --> 01:35:24.351
You shouldn't discuss the change between two states

01:35:24.351 --> 01:35:24.919
This change

01:35:24.919 --> 01:35:27.054
Instead you should discuss something

01:35:27.154 --> 01:35:29.123
Called local observable（局域可观测量）

01:35:29.123 --> 01:35:30.658
That is, the change in local observables

01:35:31.058 --> 01:35:33.060
That actually corresponds to what you see

01:35:33.060 --> 01:35:34.328
In classical physics, those changes

01:35:35.763 --> 01:35:37.264
So after four years of studying quantum physics

01:35:37.264 --> 01:35:39.500
What were you thinking at the time

01:35:40.234 --> 01:35:42.069
What do you think physics helped you with

01:35:42.970 --> 01:35:44.171
When you were about to graduate as a senior

01:35:44.572 --> 01:35:47.942
I think the biggest benefit of studying physics as an undergraduate

01:35:47.942 --> 01:35:49.710
Is first of all

01:35:50.177 --> 01:35:51.112
Think things through clearly

01:35:51.112 --> 01:35:53.080
Reading isn't about reading a lot

01:35:53.080 --> 01:35:54.014
But about reading deeply

01:35:54.615 --> 01:35:58.919
Reading a lot doesn't mean you can discover new things

01:35:59.120 --> 01:36:00.254
But if you have

01:36:00.254 --> 01:36:02.123
A perspective different from others on something

01:36:02.256 --> 01:36:04.058
That's what's more valuable

01:36:04.058 --> 01:36:05.092
To society

01:36:05.459 --> 01:36:05.960
This one thing

01:36:05.960 --> 01:36:09.130
And another thing is don't trust theory too much

01:36:09.497 --> 01:36:10.731
Don't trust pure theory too much

01:36:11.632 --> 01:36:12.199
Because

01:36:12.399 --> 01:36:13.634
I came to this conclusion

01:36:13.667 --> 01:36:16.971
Because the main reason that discovery happened at that time

01:36:16.971 --> 01:36:18.639
Was because we could do numerics

01:36:19.206 --> 01:36:21.542
It started because numerics and theory didn't match

01:36:22.076 --> 01:36:24.245
Then we carefully studied that problem

01:36:24.245 --> 01:36:25.146
And discovered this thing

01:36:27.381 --> 01:36:29.350
Then why did you go study high energy physics for your PhD

01:36:29.350 --> 01:36:30.217
That's also a theory

01:36:30.551 --> 01:36:32.119
This brings us back to the topic we just discussed

01:36:32.119 --> 01:36:34.388
That always loving to challenge very difficult things

01:36:34.889 --> 01:36:37.825
Sometimes also brings some bad results

01:36:37.825 --> 01:36:39.059
What bad results

01:36:39.059 --> 01:36:40.361
For example I feel like

01:36:40.761 --> 01:36:43.531
I think my PhD, for myself personally

01:36:44.665 --> 01:36:45.933
I learned a lot

01:36:46.033 --> 01:36:47.001
Grew a lot

01:36:47.168 --> 01:36:49.804
But for this world

01:36:49.970 --> 01:36:51.305
It didn't produce any contribution

01:36:52.373 --> 01:36:53.440
Haha, this high energy theory direction

01:36:53.440 --> 01:36:54.875
It's difficult enough

01:36:55.276 --> 01:36:56.410
Very very difficult

01:36:56.677 --> 01:36:58.813
And um

01:36:58.813 --> 01:37:00.481
But the bad thing about it is

01:37:01.448 --> 01:37:03.384
It's actually not particularly verifiable

01:37:03.818 --> 01:37:05.586
There are no objective evaluation criteria

01:37:06.220 --> 01:37:07.855
Because

01:37:07.855 --> 01:37:10.090
High energy theory has developed to the point where

01:37:10.090 --> 01:37:12.893
Experiments completely can't catch up at this stage

01:37:12.893 --> 01:37:15.429
Experiments completely can't catch up to what you're discussing in theory

01:37:15.429 --> 01:37:16.363
Whether it's energy scales

01:37:16.363 --> 01:37:18.566
Or these microscopic scales

01:37:18.799 --> 01:37:19.299
Right

01:37:19.366 --> 01:37:21.635
How does it progress

01:37:21.635 --> 01:37:23.103
What does its progress depend on

01:37:23.103 --> 01:37:24.004
If not experiments

01:37:26.507 --> 01:37:28.842
One source of progress

01:37:29.176 --> 01:37:31.812
Comes from mathematical self-consistency

01:37:31.812 --> 01:37:32.546
Mm-hmm, like for example

01:37:32.546 --> 01:37:35.883
You propose a framework

01:37:35.916 --> 01:37:36.884
To describe these things

01:37:36.884 --> 01:37:39.887
Then can you be self-consistent with existing

01:37:39.887 --> 01:37:43.224
Already verified theories at lower energy scales

01:37:43.324 --> 01:37:43.691
Like for example

01:37:43.691 --> 01:37:45.125
You study string theory

01:37:45.125 --> 01:37:46.961
Then naturally the question everyone asks is

01:37:46.994 --> 01:37:48.395
Can string theory at low energy

01:37:48.395 --> 01:37:49.597
Return to quantum field theory

01:37:49.897 --> 01:37:51.031
And then return to classical physics

01:37:51.398 --> 01:37:53.400
Then this self-consistency is one criterion

01:37:54.034 --> 01:37:55.936
I think this is very reasonable

01:37:55.936 --> 01:37:57.137
A very scientific thing

01:37:57.638 --> 01:37:59.540
Of course there are also some unscientific factors

01:37:59.540 --> 01:38:03.677
That when this field completely lacks experiments

01:38:03.677 --> 01:38:05.179
And objective standards

01:38:06.547 --> 01:38:08.549
There definitely won't be just one framework that appears

01:38:08.549 --> 01:38:10.484
There definitely won't be just one self-consistent framework that appears

01:38:10.918 --> 01:38:12.186
At this time who does well

01:38:12.186 --> 01:38:13.287
Who doesn't do well

01:38:13.621 --> 01:38:16.357
Actually depends on

01:38:16.357 --> 01:38:20.494
The subjective judgments of some old-timers in the field

01:38:20.895 --> 01:38:22.396
Did someone hurt you

01:38:22.396 --> 01:38:23.731
I wasn't hurt by anyone

01:38:23.731 --> 01:38:27.801
It's just that the longer I stayed in that field

01:38:27.801 --> 01:38:30.537
The more I felt this thing was stupid, like

01:38:32.006 --> 01:38:34.208
A person's life isn't that long

01:38:34.608 --> 01:38:36.210
Why waste your own time

01:38:36.210 --> 01:38:38.078
Serving old-timers

01:38:40.080 --> 01:38:40.881
Right

01:38:41.916 --> 01:38:46.287
So it feels like spending 5 years learning a lot of knowledge

01:38:46.287 --> 01:38:47.521
Buying a big lesson

01:38:48.122 --> 01:38:49.423
This lesson is

01:38:49.757 --> 01:38:52.726
This big lesson is to (do experiments)

01:38:52.993 --> 01:38:54.228
Hey, it's about doing

01:38:54.228 --> 01:38:57.131
Things with relatively objective evaluation criteria

01:38:57.998 --> 01:38:58.498
Mm-hmm, or from another perspective

01:38:58.532 --> 01:39:00.734
Or from another perspective

01:39:00.734 --> 01:39:01.435
Like

01:39:01.435 --> 01:39:03.971
Do things that can have an impact on this world

01:39:06.573 --> 01:39:09.143
So actually your undergraduate went relatively smoothly, right

01:39:09.143 --> 01:39:10.577
In the quantum physics research field

01:39:10.577 --> 01:39:11.378
Very quickly

01:39:11.445 --> 01:39:13.914
You very quickly had very good academic results

01:39:13.914 --> 01:39:15.449
And it was paradigm-level change

01:39:15.449 --> 01:39:17.251
But you quickly felt it wasn't attractive anymore

01:39:17.384 --> 01:39:20.354
So
You wanted to challenge something more difficult in your PhD

01:39:20.354 --> 01:39:20.754
Right

01:39:20.754 --> 01:39:23.390
And during the PhD period it was actually quite lonely

01:39:24.024 --> 01:39:25.726
At least in terms of results it was like that

01:39:25.726 --> 01:39:26.593
Hahaha

01:39:26.660 --> 01:39:27.761
The outside world couldn't tell

01:39:27.761 --> 01:39:29.129
From the outside it all looks like a very glamorous resume

01:39:29.129 --> 01:39:30.531
PhD at Stanford

01:39:30.664 --> 01:39:31.532
Right, I think

01:39:31.532 --> 01:39:34.168
In terms of actual research output

01:39:35.235 --> 01:39:35.769
I think

01:39:35.769 --> 01:39:38.672
No one would say my PhD papers were bad

01:39:39.006 --> 01:39:40.541
But if I'm being completely honest

01:39:40.541 --> 01:39:41.775
How much impact did they have on the world?

01:39:41.775 --> 01:39:42.409
I think almost none

01:39:42.409 --> 01:39:44.078
No impact, practically zero

01:39:44.912 --> 01:39:46.513
Right, so for me personally

01:39:46.513 --> 01:39:48.582
I was really unhappy with that

01:39:48.582 --> 01:39:52.853
But I also wasn't unhappy enough to, you know

01:39:52.853 --> 01:39:54.888
worry that people would say I was slacking off

01:39:55.122 --> 01:39:56.457
I really wasn't slacking off

01:39:57.858 --> 01:40:00.561
You can still meet all the external expectations

01:40:00.561 --> 01:40:01.228
Right

01:40:01.528 --> 01:40:02.563
How do you pull that off?

01:40:02.563 --> 01:40:05.165
Well, this is something that

01:40:05.165 --> 01:40:06.834
You know how it really feels, right?

01:40:06.967 --> 01:40:07.501
Right, exactly

01:40:07.501 --> 01:40:09.937
I think meeting external expectations

01:40:09.937 --> 01:40:12.039
Or meeting the standards of a small circle

01:40:12.306 --> 01:40:15.309
It's like training a model

01:40:15.476 --> 01:40:17.711
Once you're in that small circle

01:40:17.711 --> 01:40:19.346
And you know what their evaluation criteria are

01:40:19.346 --> 01:40:20.547
It's easy to do well

01:40:21.782 --> 01:40:23.217
Even if you don't actually believe in those standards

01:40:23.217 --> 01:40:24.018
You can still meet them

01:40:24.018 --> 01:40:24.518
Mhm

01:40:24.518 --> 01:40:26.186
But deep down, you know you don't buy into them

01:40:26.186 --> 01:40:29.023
Because sometimes even when you don't believe in it

01:40:29.023 --> 01:40:29.623
And you hit those marks

01:40:29.623 --> 01:40:32.760
You can fool yourself and just keep moving forward

01:40:32.860 --> 01:40:35.796
But I eventually realized I couldn't fool myself

01:40:37.664 --> 01:40:38.432
Couldn't lie to myself

01:40:38.632 --> 01:40:39.366
Mhm

01:40:39.633 --> 01:40:40.267
Right

01:40:40.401 --> 01:40:41.435
When did you realize that?

01:40:41.802 --> 01:40:43.470
I think probably around

01:40:44.872 --> 01:40:47.174
The last two years of my PhD

01:40:47.241 --> 01:40:48.842
I started having that feeling

01:40:48.842 --> 01:40:51.745
But back then, I hadn't really figured it out yet

01:40:52.012 --> 01:40:55.015
Hadn't figured out what to do if not this

01:40:55.382 --> 01:40:57.217
So I spent some time

01:40:57.217 --> 01:40:59.920
Exploring different directions

01:40:59.920 --> 01:41:02.322
For example
At first I mostly looked into

01:41:02.322 --> 01:41:04.358
Quantum computing

01:41:04.358 --> 01:41:05.793
Or quantum information, that kind of direction

01:41:06.126 --> 01:41:09.329
Then I got a postdoc offer

01:41:09.329 --> 01:41:10.798
After getting the postdoc offer

01:41:10.998 --> 01:41:13.233
It felt more urgent

01:41:13.567 --> 01:41:16.470
Because when you're still in school

01:41:16.470 --> 01:41:18.005
You can still have a student mindset

01:41:18.005 --> 01:41:20.674
After leaving school, it's your own career（事业）

01:41:21.008 --> 01:41:22.376
You have to carve out a path for yourself

01:41:23.243 --> 01:41:24.945
So at the time I felt

01:41:25.078 --> 01:41:29.216
Quantum computing and AI were probably two

01:41:29.216 --> 01:41:32.252
I think they offer young people

01:41:32.252 --> 01:41:33.620
More opportunities

01:41:34.888 --> 01:41:36.423
So what was your postdoc direction?

01:41:37.157 --> 01:41:37.891
The postdoc had no direction

01:41:37.891 --> 01:41:40.194
It was basically just theoretical physics

01:41:40.194 --> 01:41:41.862
A postdoc is a very independent position

01:41:41.862 --> 01:41:43.096
You basically do whatever you want

01:41:43.263 --> 01:41:44.498
Right, it's more like

01:41:45.799 --> 01:41:47.468
In a way, it's kind of like doing charity

01:41:48.202 --> 01:41:48.902
Huh?

01:41:48.902 --> 01:41:50.070
Who's doing charity?

01:41:50.270 --> 01:41:52.606
Well, there are probably some

01:41:53.006 --> 01:41:55.709
Whether it's government organizations that care about research

01:41:55.709 --> 01:41:56.610
Or private organizations

01:41:56.610 --> 01:41:57.311
They donate money

01:41:57.311 --> 01:41:58.378
To the university

01:41:58.712 --> 01:42:00.147
Or allocate funding to the school

01:42:00.147 --> 01:42:01.949
The school uses that money to hire postdocs

01:42:01.949 --> 01:42:04.585
Who then do research in a department

01:42:04.585 --> 01:42:05.686
And share their research

01:42:05.919 --> 01:42:07.955
Broadly with other people in the department

01:42:08.288 --> 01:42:11.725
I think it's more about creating a kind of social atmosphere

01:42:12.259 --> 01:42:12.759
This kind of

01:42:12.759 --> 01:42:13.360
This kind of work

01:42:13.694 --> 01:42:14.661
Right, and so

01:42:14.661 --> 01:42:15.662
So there really aren't many restrictions

01:42:15.662 --> 01:42:17.397
You can basically do whatever you want

01:42:17.598 --> 01:42:19.366
But I didn't actually do

01:42:19.366 --> 01:42:20.501
The postdoc for very long

01:42:20.501 --> 01:42:23.504
I was probably at Berkeley for two or three months in reality

01:42:23.504 --> 01:42:26.473
But officially, I was only there for two weeks

01:42:27.107 --> 01:42:28.242
What do you mean by officially?

01:42:28.242 --> 01:42:28.909
I mean

01:42:28.909 --> 01:42:30.410
I had actually already gone there before I officially started

01:42:30.410 --> 01:42:31.612
Because I was already in the Bay Area anyway

01:42:32.012 --> 01:42:33.180
I went there before I officially started

01:42:33.180 --> 01:42:34.414
But after I officially started

01:42:34.414 --> 01:42:35.983
I only stayed for two weeks before quitting

01:42:37.918 --> 01:42:38.986
What happened during those two weeks?

01:42:39.086 --> 01:42:40.053
Nothing happened in those two weeks

01:42:40.053 --> 01:42:41.455
I wasn't even planning to start the position

01:42:41.488 --> 01:42:42.956
But the people at Berkeley were just too nice

01:42:42.956 --> 01:42:44.258
They were like, uh

01:42:44.258 --> 01:42:45.959
No worries, just wait until things are settled

01:42:45.959 --> 01:42:47.594
Come for as long as you can

01:42:47.661 --> 01:42:50.631
Oh, so you told them you were actually talking to Anthropic

01:42:50.764 --> 01:42:51.231
Right

01:42:51.231 --> 01:42:51.832
I told them

01:42:51.832 --> 01:42:55.002
Actually I think I might go do AI

01:42:55.002 --> 01:42:56.236
Maybe I shouldn't join

01:42:56.303 --> 01:42:58.605
Mm-hmm
But Berkeley wasn't

01:42:58.605 --> 01:42:59.106
Not just Berkeley

01:42:59.106 --> 01:42:59.840
I think the Bay Area

01:42:59.840 --> 01:43:02.509
Teachers at both these schools are very nice

01:43:02.509 --> 01:43:03.176
They really take care of you

01:43:03.176 --> 01:43:05.812
They felt you haven't fully finalized things yet

01:43:05.812 --> 01:43:08.348
So better hold onto the current job first

01:43:09.449 --> 01:43:10.851
Do you think physics helped you later when doing AI

01:43:10.851 --> 01:43:11.718
In what ways

01:43:14.988 --> 01:43:16.890
I think in terms of hard skills there wasn't much help

01:43:17.357 --> 01:43:21.328
In terms of pure tool-based skills

01:43:21.328 --> 01:43:25.299
Actually the transfer from physics to AI

01:43:25.299 --> 01:43:26.533
Is very very little

01:43:27.601 --> 01:43:29.603
But I think if you really have to ask

01:43:29.603 --> 01:43:31.004
I think maybe the main

01:43:31.271 --> 01:43:32.206
Main

01:43:33.140 --> 01:43:33.907
No

01:43:33.907 --> 01:43:34.541
Can't say it's ability

01:43:34.541 --> 01:43:35.309
It's personality

01:43:35.309 --> 01:43:35.943
Maybe

01:43:35.943 --> 01:43:38.946
Maybe physics people want to get to the bottom of things more

01:43:39.446 --> 01:43:40.681
Want to understand something more

01:43:40.847 --> 01:43:42.883
And want to do things more systematically

01:43:42.883 --> 01:43:44.751
Because we're used to this very systematic

01:43:44.751 --> 01:43:45.752
Whether it's experimental methods

01:43:45.752 --> 01:43:46.920
Or theoretical methods

01:43:47.321 --> 01:43:50.290
So I think this might be

01:43:50.290 --> 01:43:51.358
A good thing

01:43:51.658 --> 01:43:55.062
But
I don't think this is unique to physics people either

01:43:55.462 --> 01:43:57.931
Like
Why wouldn't computer science people have this trait

01:43:57.931 --> 01:43:59.766
I know many computer science people

01:43:59.766 --> 01:44:00.667
Who also have this trait

01:44:01.134 --> 01:44:02.703
Many chemistry people also have this trait

01:44:02.703 --> 01:44:03.904
Biology students also have this trait

01:44:03.904 --> 01:44:05.839
So I don't think it's unique to physics

01:44:06.273 --> 01:44:08.508
Right but actually it's quite interesting

01:44:08.508 --> 01:44:10.577
There are indeed many in this field

01:44:10.577 --> 01:44:13.080
Especially with language models

01:44:13.080 --> 01:44:14.881
This kind of large scale AI

01:44:14.881 --> 01:44:17.684
There are indeed many people from physics backgrounds

01:44:17.684 --> 01:44:18.652
Who have been very successful

01:44:18.885 --> 01:44:20.654
Right especially at Anthropic this company

01:44:22.089 --> 01:44:23.890
When many people describe this generation of AI

01:44:23.890 --> 01:44:24.992
They all say it's a black box

01:44:26.093 --> 01:44:27.294
Can you use a scientific perspective

01:44:27.294 --> 01:44:28.929
To understand this black box

01:44:28.929 --> 01:44:30.597
The operating principles of artificial intelligence

01:44:30.597 --> 01:44:32.799
I think

01:44:33.767 --> 01:44:35.369
Everything in this world is a black box

01:44:36.370 --> 01:44:39.973
Like even physics

01:44:39.973 --> 01:44:41.508
Something everyone thinks they understand

01:44:41.508 --> 01:44:44.711
Actually doesn't really have

01:44:44.711 --> 01:44:47.080
An understanding from its microscopic behavior

01:44:47.080 --> 01:44:49.716
All the way to macroscopic manifestations

01:44:50.450 --> 01:44:52.319
Like whether it's quantum mechanics

01:44:52.319 --> 01:44:52.886
Or quantum field theory

01:44:52.886 --> 01:44:55.322
They all describe behavior at that energy scale

01:44:55.455 --> 01:44:56.923
Essentially the system is still a black box

01:44:56.923 --> 01:44:58.825
You still don't know at its most microscopic level

01:44:58.825 --> 01:44:59.893
What kind of dynamics

01:45:00.460 --> 01:45:01.228
AI is the same

01:45:01.228 --> 01:45:02.562
Whether it's a black box or not

01:45:02.562 --> 01:45:03.764
Is actually all relative

01:45:03.930 --> 01:45:06.667
We indeed don't understand language models to the level of

01:45:07.968 --> 01:45:09.436
Neurosurgery-level precision

01:45:09.436 --> 01:45:11.538
It's not that I understand this behavior

01:45:11.538 --> 01:45:12.272
To the extent of

01:45:12.272 --> 01:45:15.475
Saying this behavior is caused by which neuron

01:45:15.475 --> 01:45:18.345
Which artificial neuron's which activation

01:45:18.345 --> 01:45:19.279
Producing this behavior

01:45:19.713 --> 01:45:21.515
We don't have that

01:45:21.515 --> 01:45:22.449
Haven't reached that level of understanding

01:45:22.449 --> 01:45:24.351
Except in some very sparse

01:45:24.351 --> 01:45:26.253
Very small networks

01:45:26.253 --> 01:45:27.087
Like Anthropic

01:45:27.087 --> 01:45:28.989
Has this so-called Interpretability

01:45:28.989 --> 01:45:29.489
Interpretability team

01:45:29.489 --> 01:45:30.857
They might do some similar work

01:45:30.857 --> 01:45:33.293
But in practically usable language models

01:45:33.293 --> 01:45:34.628
We haven't reached such understanding

01:45:34.828 --> 01:45:36.697
But it doesn't mean we have no understanding at all

01:45:37.297 --> 01:45:38.265
For example Scaling Law

01:45:38.265 --> 01:45:41.802
It describes how models at that scale

01:45:41.802 --> 01:45:47.407
With model size and data improve in perplexity

01:45:47.407 --> 01:45:50.544
Under this metric get better and better

01:45:50.544 --> 01:45:53.146
Mm-hmm so you say there's no understanding at all

01:45:53.146 --> 01:45:54.081
Well if

01:45:54.081 --> 01:45:54.481
Scaling Law

01:45:54.481 --> 01:45:56.483
Doesn't count as a small part of understanding

01:45:56.483 --> 01:45:57.484
Then can we also say

01:45:57.484 --> 01:45:58.919
We actually don't understand this world at all either

01:45:58.919 --> 01:46:00.520
This world is also a complete black box

01:46:01.488 --> 01:46:04.725
So Scaling Law is a scientific law

01:46:05.058 --> 01:46:06.293
It's an empirical law

01:46:06.493 --> 01:46:07.527
An empirical law

01:46:07.527 --> 01:46:08.027
Right

01:46:08.128 --> 01:46:09.696
But

01:46:09.896 --> 01:46:11.798
The boundary between empirical laws and scientific laws

01:46:11.798 --> 01:46:13.633
is quite blurry

01:46:14.334 --> 01:46:16.470
For example

01:46:17.404 --> 01:46:19.439
If we look back at these thermodynamic

01:46:19.439 --> 01:46:21.308
various different laws

01:46:21.308 --> 01:46:22.609
The first law, the second law

01:46:22.609 --> 01:46:23.744
The Clapeyron equation and whatnot

01:46:23.744 --> 01:46:24.144
all this messy stuff

01:46:24.144 --> 01:46:26.747
When they were first discovered

01:46:26.747 --> 01:46:27.748
they were also empirical laws

01:46:28.648 --> 01:46:29.549
It's just that later on

01:46:29.549 --> 01:46:30.417
as time went by

01:46:30.417 --> 01:46:32.185
we gradually understood their microscopic mechanisms

01:46:32.185 --> 01:46:33.954
Then they might have become scientific laws

01:46:34.421 --> 01:46:36.390
Right, I think maybe something like Scaling Law

01:46:36.390 --> 01:46:38.225
or things like that

01:46:38.225 --> 01:46:40.827
Right now it's definitely still very impressive

01:46:41.027 --> 01:46:44.531
But in the future, when the technology becomes more fixed

01:46:44.531 --> 01:46:46.266
and people start to understand it more and more

01:46:46.266 --> 01:46:47.167
the microscopic process

01:46:47.167 --> 01:46:48.969
will it become a scientific law

01:46:48.969 --> 01:46:51.138
if such a definition exists

01:46:51.404 --> 01:46:53.173
I think it's possible

01:46:55.609 --> 01:46:57.744
Can you explain in scientific terms

01:46:57.744 --> 01:46:59.246
this so-called intelligence emergence

01:47:01.314 --> 01:47:04.484
First of all, this term itself isn't very scientific

01:47:04.751 --> 01:47:06.753
So naturally there's no way to use scientific language

01:47:06.753 --> 01:47:08.488
to describe something unscientific

01:47:08.655 --> 01:47:10.056
Intelligence emergence?

01:47:10.290 --> 01:47:13.026
Well, I think intelligence emergence

01:47:14.227 --> 01:47:17.497
to me it's more of a subjective feeling

01:47:17.497 --> 01:47:18.698
rather than an objective phenomenon

01:47:19.432 --> 01:47:21.001
When many people talk about intelligence emergence

01:47:21.001 --> 01:47:23.570
what they might have in mind is that previous language

01:47:23.570 --> 01:47:26.139
models could only do one type of thing

01:47:26.139 --> 01:47:27.174
like only translation

01:47:27.174 --> 01:47:28.308
only analysis

01:47:28.308 --> 01:47:29.042
only certain things

01:47:29.042 --> 01:47:30.410
But now it seems like the model

01:47:30.410 --> 01:47:31.411
can do everything

01:47:32.546 --> 01:47:33.713
But this thing

01:47:35.582 --> 01:47:37.717
Again, I think it's like

01:47:37.851 --> 01:47:38.718
to me

01:47:38.718 --> 01:47:40.487
it's more of a technical emergence

01:47:40.487 --> 01:47:43.190
rather than a behavioral emergence

01:47:43.457 --> 01:47:45.392
It's that through research

01:47:45.392 --> 01:47:45.826
we discovered

01:47:45.826 --> 01:47:49.262
how to do this kind of large-scale training

01:47:49.262 --> 01:47:52.232
and then be able to lift all capabilities across the board

01:47:52.466 --> 01:47:54.634
I think this is the more fundamental thing

01:47:54.835 --> 01:47:56.203
As for intelligence emergence itself

01:47:56.203 --> 01:47:58.004
Actually, I think, um

01:47:58.004 --> 01:48:00.173
everyone probably has a different definition in mind

01:48:00.373 --> 01:48:01.174
Right

01:48:01.274 --> 01:48:02.476
Your definition is

01:48:02.909 --> 01:48:04.644
To me, there's no definition

01:48:04.644 --> 01:48:06.446
Haha, to me

01:48:07.214 --> 01:48:08.915
The only qualitative difference is

01:48:08.915 --> 01:48:11.585
whether there's been a technical breakthrough

01:48:11.585 --> 01:48:13.320
that allows us to scale up

01:48:13.954 --> 01:48:15.522
and lift all capabilities across the board

01:48:15.689 --> 01:48:16.389
This, to me

01:48:16.389 --> 01:48:19.159
is a well-defined thing

01:48:19.693 --> 01:48:22.362
You ended up choosing AI

01:48:22.362 --> 01:48:23.296
between quantum computing and AI

01:48:23.563 --> 01:48:25.532
How did this shift happen

01:48:26.800 --> 01:48:28.335
Right, I think I still spent

01:48:28.335 --> 01:48:29.970
some time understanding

01:48:29.970 --> 01:48:32.105
where the bottlenecks lie in both directions

01:48:32.239 --> 01:48:34.507
I think the good thing is they both give young people opportunities

01:48:34.841 --> 01:48:35.408
The good thing is

01:48:35.408 --> 01:48:35.942
both have opportunities

01:48:35.942 --> 01:48:38.111
But quantum computing seemed to you

01:48:38.111 --> 01:48:40.347
to be closer to your main path

01:48:40.347 --> 01:48:41.114
at that time, right

01:48:41.114 --> 01:48:44.584
Well, that's why I needed to understand the details

01:48:44.584 --> 01:48:46.253
Because after understanding the details, I found out it's not

01:48:46.253 --> 01:48:47.220
It's the opposite

01:48:47.587 --> 01:48:48.588
Because quantum mechanics

01:48:48.588 --> 01:48:49.122
Oh, not quantum mechanics

01:48:49.122 --> 01:48:49.789
I mean quantum computing

01:48:49.789 --> 01:48:51.458
I think its main bottleneck right now

01:48:51.458 --> 01:48:53.360
is actually in the experiments

01:48:53.994 --> 01:48:56.563
It's not about how you design those algorithms

01:48:56.563 --> 01:48:57.497
or design those operators

01:48:57.497 --> 01:48:59.599
It's more about how you implement it experimentally

01:49:00.267 --> 01:49:01.601
That's something I'm actually not good at

01:49:01.768 --> 01:49:04.371
It's actually quite unrelated to many things

01:49:04.371 --> 01:49:05.405
I'm interested in

01:49:05.405 --> 01:49:07.807
It's actually relatively unrelated

01:49:08.174 --> 01:49:11.645
On the other hand, the things related to me are more

01:49:11.645 --> 01:49:12.712
Like AI, as I just mentioned

01:49:12.712 --> 01:49:14.781
It's more about having an idea

01:49:14.781 --> 01:49:16.316
and then you can use some numbers to verify it

01:49:16.316 --> 01:49:17.217
This numerical aspect in AI

01:49:17.217 --> 01:49:18.852
might be training a model or something like that

01:49:19.219 --> 01:49:22.422
Right and this is actually quite similar to doing physics

01:49:22.422 --> 01:49:23.390
It even is

01:49:23.423 --> 01:49:24.457
That's why

01:49:24.457 --> 01:49:26.226
I've always liked to compare this

01:49:26.226 --> 01:49:28.094
With 18th century physics

01:49:28.094 --> 01:49:29.229
Make comparisons

01:49:29.229 --> 01:49:32.165
It's more like physics of that era

01:49:32.165 --> 01:49:34.167
In that era theory and experiment weren't separated

01:49:34.401 --> 01:49:35.702
There were no theoretical physicists

01:49:35.702 --> 01:49:36.636
Experimental physicists

01:49:36.770 --> 01:49:37.437
You just did physics

01:49:37.437 --> 01:49:38.238
Just did physics

01:49:38.305 --> 01:49:40.040
You could do experiments yourself

01:49:40.106 --> 01:49:41.775
And also do theoretical speculation

01:49:41.808 --> 01:49:43.343
I think AI is a bit like that era

01:49:43.410 --> 01:49:45.278
So actually

01:49:45.312 --> 01:49:48.348
The distance from theoretical physics to experimental physics

01:49:48.348 --> 01:49:50.216
Is farther than directly jumping to AI

01:49:50.483 --> 01:49:51.518
Farther, mm-hmm

01:49:51.585 --> 01:49:52.352
Actually farther

01:49:52.352 --> 01:49:54.187
And in terms of interest it's also farther

01:49:54.220 --> 01:49:55.722
You don't like experimental physics

01:49:56.056 --> 01:49:57.057
(I think) You don't like doing experiments

01:49:57.257 --> 01:49:59.159
I think, um

01:49:59.326 --> 01:50:01.394
It's indeed not where my interest lies

01:50:01.928 --> 01:50:03.129
Mm-hmm although I'm not willing to do it myself

01:50:03.129 --> 01:50:04.197
But I am indeed very interested

01:50:04.197 --> 01:50:05.632
In knowing how other people's experiments are going

01:50:05.632 --> 01:50:08.702
Hahahaha

01:50:08.702 --> 01:50:10.203
Doesn't AI require doing experiments

01:50:10.203 --> 01:50:12.038
Yes, but it's more like numerics

01:50:12.405 --> 01:50:14.107
Right it's not quite like

01:50:14.107 --> 01:50:17.344
That thing where you go to the lab and build an optical table

01:50:17.344 --> 01:50:18.044
And whatnot

01:50:18.044 --> 01:50:19.546
You also have to

01:50:19.546 --> 01:50:21.114
I think experiments are really something

01:50:21.348 --> 01:50:22.916
Maybe because I don't understand

01:50:22.949 --> 01:50:24.784
I haven't reached that level

01:50:24.784 --> 01:50:28.488
So some things seem quite mystical to me

01:50:28.688 --> 01:50:29.322
For example

01:50:29.322 --> 01:50:31.758
Everyone knows how to build this optical table

01:50:32.158 --> 01:50:34.260
But some people can build it for you

01:50:34.494 --> 01:50:36.663
Some people just can't build it after 6 years

01:50:37.297 --> 01:50:38.932
This is hands-on ability

01:50:39.132 --> 01:50:40.266
I just don't get it

01:50:40.266 --> 01:50:42.135
Hahahaha

01:50:42.135 --> 01:50:42.869
I sometimes think

01:50:42.869 --> 01:50:44.771
This thing is a bit mystical

01:50:45.472 --> 01:50:45.972
Oh

01:50:46.706 --> 01:50:49.275
Mm-hmm so numerics are still better

01:50:49.275 --> 01:50:51.277
Numerics are much clearer

01:50:51.578 --> 01:50:52.679
Right right right, for me

01:50:52.846 --> 01:50:54.581
Doing numerical experiments

01:50:54.581 --> 01:50:55.215
Or like AI

01:50:55.215 --> 01:50:56.182
Training models

01:50:56.182 --> 01:50:58.418
And studying various different techniques

01:50:58.418 --> 01:50:59.452
To look at certain details

01:50:59.452 --> 01:51:02.756
This thing is actually um, is

01:51:02.756 --> 01:51:05.492
I can understand why it's done this way

01:51:06.559 --> 01:51:08.328
Mm-hmm but when it comes to building the table

01:51:08.328 --> 01:51:10.630
I'm completely at a loss

01:51:10.630 --> 01:51:11.498
You've done it before

01:51:12.999 --> 01:51:14.200
I of course have

01:51:14.200 --> 01:51:15.635
Everyone has probably done basic

01:51:15.635 --> 01:51:17.370
Physics students definitely all

01:51:17.370 --> 01:51:18.905
