02:03:04.343 --> 02:03:05.077
And then he left

02:03:05.077 --> 02:03:06.045
So...

02:03:07.713 --> 02:03:08.881
What about other companies?

02:03:09.014 --> 02:03:11.050
I think other companies all find it pretty difficult

02:03:11.050 --> 02:03:13.119
Even Gemini finds it pretty difficult

02:03:13.119 --> 02:03:15.254
But I think Gemini has a completely different playbook

02:03:15.254 --> 02:03:15.688
It's a bit different

02:03:15.688 --> 02:03:17.223
That is, um

02:03:17.223 --> 02:03:19.959
I think big companies and startups

02:03:20.092 --> 02:03:21.961
Their playbooks are fundamentally different

02:03:21.961 --> 02:03:25.231
Because for startups, what's important is to make bets

02:03:25.398 --> 02:03:27.299
That is, I have to bet on something

02:03:27.933 --> 02:03:29.402
If I want to bet

02:03:29.402 --> 02:03:30.503
It means there's risk

02:03:31.203 --> 02:03:33.639
So that means

02:03:33.639 --> 02:03:36.909
I can make decisions very quickly

02:03:36.909 --> 02:03:38.511
And push decisions through strongly

02:03:38.511 --> 02:03:40.212
So perhaps in this situation

02:03:40.212 --> 02:03:42.448
Top-down is a big advantage, I think

02:03:42.515 --> 02:03:44.483
So I think organizationally, Anthropic

02:03:44.483 --> 02:03:45.718
Has an advantage over OpenAI

02:03:46.285 --> 02:03:47.453
But as a big company

02:03:47.453 --> 02:03:49.054
It might have a different mindset

02:03:49.221 --> 02:03:50.689
Because a big company's mindset might be

02:03:51.257 --> 02:03:54.994
Not only can I minimize the gambling aspect

02:03:55.327 --> 02:03:58.397
But I can also have reserves in every area

02:03:58.664 --> 02:04:00.366
And then if anything succeeds

02:04:00.366 --> 02:04:01.233
I can catch up

02:04:01.767 --> 02:04:03.369
And if I succeed at something myself

02:04:03.369 --> 02:04:04.403
I might even take the lead

02:04:04.670 --> 02:04:05.971
That's probably the big company mindset

02:04:06.071 --> 02:04:07.273
So at Gemini

02:04:07.406 --> 02:04:08.774
Google is a very traditional

02:04:08.774 --> 02:04:10.075
Very bottom-up organization

02:04:10.709 --> 02:04:11.977
At the company level

02:04:11.977 --> 02:04:14.847
There may be some well-defined frameworks

02:04:14.847 --> 02:04:17.716
To evaluate whether your work is good or bad

02:04:17.716 --> 02:04:21.020
To guide you to do things the company needs

02:04:21.020 --> 02:04:21.654
But essentially

02:04:21.654 --> 02:04:23.222
It's still you deciding what you do yourself

02:04:23.322 --> 02:04:26.458
So you think Anthropic can make bets (referring to betting heavily on coding)

02:04:26.458 --> 02:04:28.661
Because of its unique culture

02:04:29.228 --> 02:04:30.596
Organization and culture, yes

02:04:32.998 --> 02:04:34.099
This sounds like

02:04:34.099 --> 02:04:35.801
