02:16:53.371 --> 02:16:55.006
Right you can actually teach it many things

02:16:55.006 --> 02:16:56.675
Right but we humans as teachers

02:16:56.675 --> 02:16:58.410
Now don't know what the next thing to teach is

02:16:58.410 --> 02:16:59.010
Right right

02:16:59.010 --> 02:17:00.912
Or how to reasonably teach it

02:17:01.046 --> 02:17:02.714
Using current paradigms

02:17:04.683 --> 02:17:07.285
Speaking of 3.7, what other know-how

02:17:07.986 --> 02:17:10.288
How many months did this take

02:17:11.389 --> 02:17:15.093
This finally all in all

02:17:15.093 --> 02:17:16.962
From starting training to release

02:17:16.962 --> 02:17:19.864
Probably took about four or five months

02:17:20.298 --> 02:17:22.400
From when you first joined

02:17:22.400 --> 02:17:23.969
From when everyone started

02:17:23.969 --> 02:17:26.271
Doing research for this thing

02:17:26.471 --> 02:17:27.806
That probably took two or three months

02:17:27.806 --> 02:17:30.542
And then later from starting training to training completion

02:17:30.542 --> 02:17:31.409
With bumps along the way

02:17:31.409 --> 02:17:32.544
Many things to handle

02:17:32.544 --> 02:17:35.146
And there was a lot of new infrastructure

02:17:35.146 --> 02:17:36.681
Actually infrastructure is really important

02:17:36.681 --> 02:17:37.582
Very time-consuming

02:17:37.616 --> 02:17:40.685
And then probably took about two months or so

02:17:40.685 --> 02:17:41.486
What important work did you do in it

02:17:41.486 --> 02:17:42.687
I don't think I did anything important

02:17:42.687 --> 02:17:44.122
Hahaha

02:17:44.155 --> 02:17:46.791
I think

02:17:47.158 --> 02:17:47.993
My personal contribution

02:17:47.993 --> 02:17:50.428
I personally

02:17:52.330 --> 02:17:53.832
My contribution to any model

02:17:53.832 --> 02:17:55.133
My statement

02:17:55.133 --> 02:17:56.835
Is always

02:17:56.835 --> 02:17:57.302
I feel like I'm not that important to that thing

02:17:57.302 --> 02:17:59.471
I think more importantly I was very lucky

02:17:59.471 --> 02:18:02.407
To have the opportunity

02:18:02.407 --> 02:18:03.274
To join an important project at that time

02:18:03.274 --> 02:18:06.378
And did some things

02:18:06.544 --> 02:18:07.479
Mm-hmm, because in a sense

02:18:07.946 --> 02:18:10.482
I think AI in recent years

02:18:10.482 --> 02:18:14.219
This thing itself is unstoppable

02:18:14.686 --> 02:18:17.322
It doesn't depend on whether you do it or not

02:18:18.623 --> 02:18:20.992
If you don't do it someone else can do it just as well

02:18:20.992 --> 02:18:23.895
So I think in this era

02:18:23.895 --> 02:18:25.764
Actually all things that give individuals credit

02:18:25.764 --> 02:18:29.000
Are somewhat hyped

02:18:29.000 --> 02:18:30.235
Suspicious

02:18:30.235 --> 02:18:31.302
Of being hyped

02:18:31.302 --> 02:18:33.071
But indeed I think for me

02:18:33.071 --> 02:18:33.872
I am very lucky

02:18:33.872 --> 02:18:36.508
Being able to join at that stage was a big deal

02:18:36.608 --> 02:18:38.910
And, well, I learned a few things

02:18:38.910 --> 02:18:41.246
So you were lucky to be there at that stage

02:18:41.246 --> 02:18:42.447
At Anthropic

02:18:42.447 --> 02:18:44.316
this company's

02:18:44.382 --> 02:18:47.552
large-scale reinforcement learning team

02:18:47.585 --> 02:18:48.520
what did you do

02:18:48.586 --> 02:18:51.056
I think around the 3.7 era, what we mainly worked on was still

02:18:51.056 --> 02:18:54.859
working on this agentic coding thing

02:18:54.893 --> 02:18:56.861
how to scale this thing up

02:18:56.861 --> 02:18:58.463
or how to prepare

02:18:58.496 --> 02:18:59.698
like how to set up

02:18:59.698 --> 02:19:02.067
all kinds of environments and data

02:19:02.067 --> 02:19:03.735
including what algorithmic problems you'd run into

02:19:03.735 --> 02:19:05.236
Most of the research at the time was on this part

02:19:05.503 --> 02:19:06.638
Any tips on this?

02:19:10.375 --> 02:19:12.077
Looking back, there aren't really any particularly useful tips, haha

02:19:12.944 --> 02:19:15.146
I think

02:19:15.346 --> 02:19:16.748
When it comes to technical tips

02:19:16.748 --> 02:19:17.849
this is actually something

02:19:17.916 --> 02:19:21.252
that on one hand, people are really eager to hear about

02:19:21.453 --> 02:19:22.687
but companies won't let you talk about

02:19:22.687 --> 02:19:24.389
and in reality isn't very useful

02:19:24.723 --> 02:19:25.290
Why?

02:19:25.290 --> 02:19:27.959
Because a lot of algorithm design isn't actually independent

02:19:27.959 --> 02:19:29.094
independent of the algorithm itself

02:19:29.094 --> 02:19:30.795
It's very strongly

02:19:30.795 --> 02:19:32.130
dependent on your infrastructure

02:19:32.530 --> 02:19:33.932
A simple example is

02:19:34.199 --> 02:19:35.133
some companies

02:19:35.133 --> 02:19:36.868
there's a problem people often discuss

02:19:36.868 --> 02:19:38.870
which is during reinforcement learning

02:19:38.870 --> 02:19:42.307
the sample（采样） machine, the one that generates these

02:19:42.307 --> 02:19:42.907
these trace（轨迹）

02:19:42.907 --> 02:19:46.111
these token(词元) — that machine and the trainer(训练器)

02:19:46.111 --> 02:19:47.445
used to actually train the model

02:19:47.445 --> 02:19:49.981
and then update the model weights — that machine

02:19:50.048 --> 02:19:52.584
these two machines might be different

02:19:53.718 --> 02:19:54.686
But the difference

02:19:54.686 --> 02:19:56.388
is partly due to numerical differences

02:19:56.388 --> 02:19:58.323
and partly because

02:19:58.323 --> 02:20:00.091
of using this kind of asynchronous training architecture

02:20:00.091 --> 02:20:01.760
so naturally

02:20:01.760 --> 02:20:03.061
fundamentally they're different

02:20:03.194 --> 02:20:06.131
So different companies might have different

02:20:06.131 --> 02:20:07.065
degrees of this difference

02:20:07.465 --> 02:20:09.367
so your algorithm design will also differ

02:20:09.701 --> 02:20:12.404
Some companies might have these two differences

02:20:12.404 --> 02:20:14.072
being very, very large

02:20:14.072 --> 02:20:16.474
then the biggest part of your algorithm might be

02:20:16.474 --> 02:20:17.475
how to control this

02:20:17.475 --> 02:20:19.277
and how to keep the training stable

02:20:19.277 --> 02:20:23.748
Things like the actual training effectiveness

02:20:23.948 --> 02:20:25.550
will be weighted slightly less

02:20:25.750 --> 02:20:26.684
But some companies might

02:20:26.684 --> 02:20:29.387
have particularly excellent infrastructure

02:20:29.487 --> 02:20:30.655
so the difference between these two isn't that big

02:20:30.655 --> 02:20:31.856
then you can probably spend more effort

02:20:31.856 --> 02:20:33.458
on the training effectiveness

02:20:33.725 --> 02:20:35.894
So a lot of these small tips

02:20:35.894 --> 02:20:37.762
are actually not very useful

02:20:37.762 --> 02:20:39.464
A lot of know-how is actually not very useful

02:20:40.331 --> 02:20:44.135
I say this because I've indeed noticed

02:20:44.135 --> 02:20:45.203
that many

02:20:45.303 --> 02:20:47.772
other labs — well, not

02:20:47.772 --> 02:20:50.542
people in these three labs probably really want to know

02:20:50.542 --> 02:20:51.676
like how Anthropic does this

02:20:51.676 --> 02:20:52.844
or how Gemini does that

02:20:53.311 --> 02:20:54.712
But sometimes I'm reluctant to answer

02:20:54.712 --> 02:20:55.313
One main reason

02:20:55.313 --> 02:20:57.882
is that fundamentally I think

02:20:57.882 --> 02:20:59.651
answering this question would mislead them

02:21:00.518 --> 02:21:03.288
Modern AI training is a large system

02:21:03.288 --> 02:21:06.191
You actually need to understand

02:21:06.191 --> 02:21:07.492
all aspects of this system

02:21:07.492 --> 02:21:08.927
to have a holistic understanding

02:21:08.927 --> 02:21:11.396
of what makes something useful because of what

02:21:11.462 --> 02:21:13.398
rather than saying the thing itself is useful

02:21:14.966 --> 02:21:17.469
What happened from 3.7 to 4.5?

02:21:17.869 --> 02:21:20.338
Both pre-training and post-training, yes

02:21:20.338 --> 02:21:21.739
And, um

02:21:21.739 --> 02:21:22.774
Of course it's just

02:21:22.774 --> 02:21:24.976
more scaling up

02:21:24.976 --> 02:21:25.643
And data

02:21:25.643 --> 02:21:27.645
Whether it's data or training

02:21:27.846 --> 02:21:32.050
the compute is at a much larger scale

02:21:32.050 --> 02:21:34.285
But I think in terms of paradigm, there wasn't

02:21:34.686 --> 02:21:37.755
anything particularly major that changed

02:21:39.958 --> 02:21:41.960
How many people was it when you left Anthropic?

02:21:43.862 --> 02:21:45.029
Close to 2,000, I think

02:21:45.096 --> 02:21:46.130
More than doubled

02:21:46.130 --> 02:21:47.265
Ah, um

02:21:47.465 --> 02:21:49.033
So during your time at Anthropic

02:21:49.033 --> 02:21:52.604
it happened to be going through its most dramatic transformation

02:21:52.937 --> 02:21:54.339
Ah, I probably just caught

02:21:54.339 --> 02:21:57.041
the tail end of it being a small company

02:21:57.108 --> 02:22:00.879
Actually, I think after three

02:22:00.879 --> 02:22:02.847
or four months, the company already started

02:22:02.847 --> 02:22:04.382
and suddenly there were way more people

02:22:04.382 --> 02:22:05.416
Did the culture change?

02:22:06.117 --> 02:22:08.586
There were still some rather chaotic phases

02:22:08.620 --> 02:22:09.420
And then

02:22:09.420 --> 02:22:12.523
Especially around the time when I left

02:22:12.523 --> 02:22:13.424
The period right before I left

02:22:13.424 --> 02:22:15.527
I think culturally, it went through some

02:22:15.527 --> 02:22:17.228
some chaos

02:22:17.228 --> 02:22:19.597
Because some people came in from outside

02:22:19.597 --> 02:22:22.133
and there was probably some conflict with the original culture

02:22:23.534 --> 02:22:25.069
Oh, the previous culture was

02:22:25.470 --> 02:22:26.404
I think before, it was just

02:22:26.404 --> 02:22:27.105
pretty simple

02:22:27.105 --> 02:22:27.705
Yeah, it was very simple

02:22:27.705 --> 02:22:28.406
It was

02:22:28.406 --> 02:22:30.541
more like a small workshop

02:22:30.742 --> 02:22:31.776
Everyone was friends

02:22:31.776 --> 02:22:33.745
And everyone knew what the others were doing

02:22:33.745 --> 02:22:34.879
And

02:22:34.879 --> 02:22:38.116
No one was particularly

02:22:38.116 --> 02:22:39.250
you know, doing

02:22:39.250 --> 02:22:41.853
too much self-promotion or anything like that

02:22:41.853 --> 02:22:42.954
Doing pointless things

02:22:42.954 --> 02:22:44.122
No one was doing pointless things

02:22:44.122 --> 02:22:45.990
Everyone had a lot on their plate

02:22:46.124 --> 02:22:47.692
And the company back then

02:22:47.692 --> 02:22:49.193
probably had a stronger sense of urgency

02:22:49.527 --> 02:22:51.796
And later on, people probably felt that

02:22:51.796 --> 02:22:52.730
with more people

02:22:52.730 --> 02:22:54.399
this kind of culture would definitely take some hits

02:22:56.567 --> 02:22:57.835
What kind of atmosphere did it bring?

02:22:59.370 --> 02:23:00.405
I think

02:23:00.405 --> 02:23:05.310
There were indeed some people I personally didn't like very much

02:23:05.310 --> 02:23:07.312
Of course, that doesn't mean they're actually bad

02:23:07.312 --> 02:23:08.212
I'm just saying I personally didn't like them

02:23:08.212 --> 02:23:11.082
I mean, I probably don't like

02:23:11.316 --> 02:23:14.018
people who talk a lot in this field

02:23:16.754 --> 02:23:19.290
Like, I think 'idea is cheap'

02:23:19.290 --> 02:23:21.125
Ideas are cheap

02:23:21.125 --> 02:23:21.659
Many ideas

02:23:21.659 --> 02:23:23.161
are actually quite obvious, everyone knows them

02:23:23.161 --> 02:23:24.662
The hard part is how to implement them

02:23:24.896 --> 02:23:26.297
How to break it down into small

02:23:26.297 --> 02:23:27.165
actionable steps

02:23:27.165 --> 02:23:27.966
and actually get it done

02:23:28.633 --> 02:23:31.836
I don't think I like those

02:23:32.270 --> 02:23:34.505
who spend a large part of their day

02:23:34.505 --> 02:23:35.573
on Slack, I mean Slack

02:23:35.573 --> 02:23:37.508
is a workplace software used in the US

02:23:37.508 --> 02:23:39.077
and spending a lot of time on Slack

02:23:39.077 --> 02:23:42.146
talking about grand principles

02:23:42.547 --> 02:23:43.781
I think it's just

02:23:45.116 --> 02:23:47.085
not very useful, haha

02:23:49.287 --> 02:23:50.788
Why did you suddenly leave later on?

02:23:50.822 --> 02:23:52.623
Had you completed some milestone at the time?

02:23:53.424 --> 02:23:54.926
How long had you been thinking about it?

02:23:55.727 --> 02:23:58.029
At the time, I think I'd been thinking about it for

02:23:59.397 --> 02:24:00.064
a month or two

02:24:00.064 --> 02:24:00.631
about a month or so

02:24:00.631 --> 02:24:01.532
a little over a month

02:24:01.532 --> 02:24:03.935
That was fast, yeah yeah

02:24:03.935 --> 02:24:06.571
I think one aspect was

02:24:06.571 --> 02:24:08.339
Um, it was

02:24:08.406 --> 02:24:13.344
I actually didn't really agree with Dario's anti-China stance

02:24:13.778 --> 02:24:19.083
Ah, I think as a company CEO

02:24:19.083 --> 02:24:20.151
For him personally

02:24:20.151 --> 02:24:22.420
whatever views he holds, I think it's fine

02:24:22.654 --> 02:24:24.522
But as a company CEO

02:24:24.522 --> 02:24:25.323
I think

02:24:25.323 --> 02:24:28.192
pushing this view to such an extreme

02:24:28.192 --> 02:24:29.994
was a very emotional reaction

02:24:30.395 --> 02:24:33.464
Yeah, and this was a relatively minor reason

02:24:33.464 --> 02:24:34.132
But on the bigger picture

02:24:34.132 --> 02:24:34.932
There are many companies

02:24:34.932 --> 02:24:35.767
Like I just mentioned

02:24:35.867 --> 02:24:37.402
There were some cultural shocks at the company

02:24:37.402 --> 02:24:38.670
And including myself

02:24:38.670 --> 02:24:42.674
I probably wanted to learn some different things

02:24:42.774 --> 02:24:43.808
I mean, Anthropic

02:24:43.808 --> 02:24:45.810
is after all very focused

02:24:45.943 --> 02:24:47.078
And you might be doing

02:24:47.078 --> 02:24:48.646
If you really want to work on everything related to language

02:24:48.646 --> 02:24:49.847
models in all aspects

02:24:49.847 --> 02:24:50.448
And

02:24:50.448 --> 02:24:53.885
working on this kind of tool use, this Agentic stuff

02:24:53.885 --> 02:24:54.852
and coding and such

02:24:54.852 --> 02:24:56.387
then Anthropic is actually great

02:24:56.387 --> 02:24:57.255
You can learn a lot

02:24:57.255 --> 02:24:58.823
But there are many things Anthropic doesn't do

02:24:59.023 --> 02:25:01.159
For example, no one at Anthropic is doing

02:25:01.159 --> 02:25:03.027
this kind of multimodal generation

02:25:03.327 --> 02:25:04.395
You want to learn but there's nowhere to learn it

02:25:04.762 --> 02:25:06.931
And Anthropic probably didn't spend too much energy

02:25:06.931 --> 02:25:08.766
on this kind of more low-level

02:25:08.766 --> 02:25:10.034
engineering

02:25:10.034 --> 02:25:11.803
infrastructure

02:25:12.036 --> 02:25:12.370
Right

02:25:12.370 --> 02:25:16.007
So probably wanting to learn more things

02:25:16.007 --> 02:25:17.775
was also one of my motivations for leaving at the time

02:25:19.744 --> 02:25:21.446
What percentage was the anti-China stance?

02:25:22.180 --> 02:25:23.648
Because of Dario's personal reasons

02:25:23.648 --> 02:25:24.415
I've in public

02:25:24.415 --> 02:25:25.383
Combined say 40%

02:25:25.383 --> 02:25:28.453
But this number anyway just listen to it

02:25:28.586 --> 02:25:29.454
This number just tells you

02:25:29.454 --> 02:25:30.755
It's not the main reason

02:25:30.788 --> 02:25:32.457
But it is indeed a very big reason

02:25:33.558 --> 02:25:34.225
Not controlling

02:25:34.225 --> 02:25:35.059
Not a controlling reason

02:25:35.059 --> 02:25:36.160
Right not a controlling reason

02:25:36.160 --> 02:25:40.298
But it's a majority holder reason

02:25:42.834 --> 02:25:44.836
Your choice is also quite amazing

02:25:44.836 --> 02:25:45.603
Because most people

02:25:45.603 --> 02:25:50.007
When it's still an underdog

02:25:50.007 --> 02:25:51.275
Joining will create more emotional attachment

02:25:51.275 --> 02:25:53.644
Willing to accompany the company for a longer time

02:25:53.745 --> 02:25:56.814
But you instead jumped to Google

02:25:56.814 --> 02:25:58.783
Because many researchers once they enter Google

02:25:58.783 --> 02:26:02.587
They feel Google doesn't give enough scope

02:26:02.587 --> 02:26:03.254
Mm-hmm

02:26:03.254 --> 02:26:05.756
So they instead want to jump to places like xAI

02:26:05.756 --> 02:26:08.459
Or smaller organizations like Anthropic

02:26:08.459 --> 02:26:11.229
Your move seems to be the opposite

02:26:11.229 --> 02:26:12.830
Right I think

02:26:12.830 --> 02:26:14.732
Actually depends on what you yourself want

02:26:14.732 --> 02:26:18.069
If what you really want is I have a very clear

02:26:18.069 --> 02:26:19.637
Like you said a very clear scope

02:26:19.837 --> 02:26:20.805
And this thing

02:26:20.805 --> 02:26:23.941
Is closely related to my final product model

02:26:23.941 --> 02:26:26.611
I must get one of my ideas

02:26:27.378 --> 02:26:28.646
Into this model

02:26:29.046 --> 02:26:31.215
Then Google might be a very bad place

02:26:31.616 --> 02:26:33.851
Because after all there are so many researchers

02:26:33.851 --> 02:26:35.553
So many already mature organizations

02:26:35.653 --> 02:26:37.655
Doing this thing

02:26:37.655 --> 02:26:39.657
Has a very complicated process

02:26:40.591 --> 02:26:42.960
But I think Gemini is very

02:26:43.127 --> 02:26:46.330
If what you want is research freedom

02:26:46.330 --> 02:26:47.632
Freedom to explore

02:26:47.632 --> 02:26:51.869
And want to learn from broader humanity

02:26:52.069 --> 02:26:52.970
I think in this world

02:26:52.970 --> 02:26:54.972
You probably can't find a second place stronger than Gemini

02:26:56.641 --> 02:26:57.475
So

02:26:58.776 --> 02:26:59.644
So it's

02:26:59.644 --> 02:27:00.211
I think

02:27:00.211 --> 02:27:02.680
Essentially it still depends on what you yourself want

02:27:03.447 --> 02:27:05.683
But I think many people when they leave

02:27:05.683 --> 02:27:07.051
Regardless of where they leave from

02:27:07.051 --> 02:27:08.152
After switching to another place

02:27:08.152 --> 02:27:10.087
The main reason they might feel unhappy

02:27:10.087 --> 02:27:11.622
Is because they didn't figure out what they wanted

02:27:11.622 --> 02:27:14.692
For example if you came to Google

02:27:14.759 --> 02:27:15.993
But told me

02:27:15.993 --> 02:27:18.229
At first you thought you wanted research freedom

02:27:18.229 --> 02:27:20.665
And more motivation was learning

02:27:20.665 --> 02:27:21.332
And after you went

02:27:21.332 --> 02:27:24.869
Discovered you still wanted product impact

02:27:25.169 --> 02:27:27.038
Then you might feel very uncomfortable haha

02:27:27.838 --> 02:27:29.574
You don't pursue impact

02:27:29.841 --> 02:27:31.275
You also said this

02:27:31.275 --> 02:27:33.511
Now AI is a very large system

02:27:33.511 --> 02:27:35.012
And is a

02:27:35.012 --> 02:27:38.216
Very large collaborative effort

02:27:38.482 --> 02:27:39.584
What are you pursuing in it

02:27:39.650 --> 02:27:40.885
I think it's divided into stages

02:27:40.885 --> 02:27:41.686
I think

02:27:42.220 --> 02:27:43.287
At Anthropic

02:27:43.287 --> 02:27:44.622
After experiencing too much

02:27:44.622 --> 02:27:48.726
Product-related things

02:27:48.726 --> 02:27:50.995
I might also want to change my mindset

02:27:51.262 --> 02:27:53.164
To learn some different things

02:27:53.297 --> 02:27:54.365
But you say is there any day

02:27:54.365 --> 02:27:55.867
I might switch back to this mindset

02:27:55.867 --> 02:27:58.236
And want to produce some product influence

02:27:58.236 --> 02:27:59.103
That's also possible

02:27:59.971 --> 02:28:01.572
How do you quantify product influence

02:28:02.073 --> 02:28:03.307
This is very clear internally

02:28:03.307 --> 02:28:04.108
Really

02:28:04.275 --> 02:28:05.276
Hard to quantify

02:28:05.476 --> 02:28:06.344
I think

02:28:06.344 --> 02:28:09.180
Because when publishing papers there was still first author

02:28:09.180 --> 02:28:10.848
This kind of lead author

02:28:11.282 --> 02:28:12.416
Now

02:28:12.416 --> 02:28:14.185
Mm-hmm actually there's no way to quantify

02:28:14.185 --> 02:28:15.419
The reality is there's no way to quantify

02:28:15.419 --> 02:28:18.489
This is also why I think in this era

02:28:18.489 --> 02:28:20.958
Actually talking about each individual's influence

02:28:20.958 --> 02:28:23.995
Is a very very ethereal thing

02:28:24.695 --> 02:28:28.132
I think essentially it's still the organization that did

02:28:28.132 --> 02:28:29.000
Such a thing

02:28:29.367 --> 02:28:30.534
Or the world needs this

02:28:30.534 --> 02:28:32.770
So producing product impact is a subjective feeling

02:28:32.937 --> 02:28:36.007
At least on the model side it is

02:28:36.007 --> 02:28:37.475
Right and then

02:28:37.475 --> 02:28:38.843
Of course actually you can

02:28:38.843 --> 02:28:39.543
I think you can

02:28:39.543 --> 02:28:44.148
The details are about what things you yourself have done

02:28:44.148 --> 02:28:45.449
Specific technical contributions

02:28:45.449 --> 02:28:47.385
And the effects produced technically

02:28:47.451 --> 02:28:49.553
This can be discussed objectively

02:28:49.687 --> 02:28:50.988
But more subjective things are

02:28:50.988 --> 02:28:51.422
You were saying

02:28:51.422 --> 02:28:53.791
how much did this effect account for in the final product

02:28:53.791 --> 02:28:56.861
No one can really say for sure

02:28:57.194 --> 02:28:59.196
Can you describe what you did on 3.7

02:28:59.864 --> 02:29:01.666
What kind of technical work did you do

02:29:01.666 --> 02:29:03.134
that actually had an impact on the model

02:29:03.567 --> 02:29:04.735
It was mainly related to agentic coding

02:29:04.735 --> 02:29:08.039
and the environment around it

02:29:08.039 --> 02:29:10.341
And some algorithmic work as well

02:29:10.341 --> 02:29:13.144
On the algorithmic side, it was mainly about making the training more

02:29:14.011 --> 02:29:14.812
stable

02:29:14.812 --> 02:29:16.981
To be honest

02:29:17.181 --> 02:29:20.685
But I do think there were definitely some algorithmic improvements

02:29:20.685 --> 02:29:22.453
but they didn't achieve particularly ideal results

02:29:22.453 --> 02:29:23.554
To be honest

02:29:23.554 --> 02:29:26.223
It's definitely better than the previous algorithms

02:29:26.557 --> 02:29:27.024
Yeah

02:29:27.024 --> 02:29:29.627
But I don't think that was my personal contribution

02:29:30.161 --> 02:29:32.530
I think it was a collective effort from everyone, haha

02:29:32.830 --> 02:29:33.864
Right, every time I ask you

02:29:33.864 --> 02:29:35.666
you always say it's a collective effort

02:29:35.666 --> 02:29:39.170
It's not an era of individual heroism anymore

02:29:39.170 --> 02:29:41.806
Right, I think the era of individual heroism

02:29:42.606 --> 02:29:43.774
for language models

02:29:43.774 --> 02:29:45.376
has probably passed

02:29:45.376 --> 02:29:46.143
When was it?

02:29:46.310 --> 02:29:48.279
It was the Transformer moment

02:29:48.279 --> 02:29:49.780
Right, at that point when the technology

02:29:49.780 --> 02:29:52.283
hadn't yet reached the scale-up stage

02:29:52.483 --> 02:29:54.018
The person who discovered that technology

02:29:54.018 --> 02:29:55.019
might be a hero

02:29:55.019 --> 02:29:56.620
Or a small group that discovered it

02:29:56.620 --> 02:29:57.555
might be heroes

02:29:57.822 --> 02:29:58.656
After that technology was found

02:29:58.656 --> 02:29:59.457
for probably a long time

02:29:59.457 --> 02:30:01.092
from the model side, it's all been

02:30:01.092 --> 02:30:02.460
I think more about collectivism

02:30:02.827 --> 02:30:05.663
whether this group can work together

02:30:05.663 --> 02:30:07.231
whether they can toward a common goal

02:30:07.531 --> 02:30:09.200
spending their own time together

02:30:09.200 --> 02:30:10.167
and their own energy

02:30:10.234 --> 02:30:11.602
That's the most important thing

02:30:11.802 --> 02:30:13.037
Rather than what each individual

02:30:13.037 --> 02:30:14.271
contributed

02:30:15.873 --> 02:30:17.174
The reason you say collectivism

02:30:17.174 --> 02:30:20.311
is because the capability actually comes from AI, is that right?

02:30:20.578 --> 02:30:21.679
The reason I say collectivism

02:30:21.679 --> 02:30:24.615
is because I think AI as a field is fundamentally simple

02:30:24.615 --> 02:30:26.350
Like

02:30:26.350 --> 02:30:27.685
I don't think there's any

02:30:27.985 --> 02:30:29.820
Except maybe that leap moment

02:30:29.954 --> 02:30:31.222
where the idea might require

02:30:31.222 --> 02:30:32.757
some really deep insights

02:30:32.923 --> 02:30:33.891
In the process after that

02:30:33.891 --> 02:30:36.894
many ideas are actually very trivial (微不足道的)

02:30:36.894 --> 02:30:39.697
Very stupid, basically

02:30:39.697 --> 02:30:40.498
Anyone could think of them

02:30:40.498 --> 02:30:41.399
Anyone could do them

02:30:41.732 --> 02:30:43.067
It's just that you got lucky

02:30:43.067 --> 02:30:44.402
and happened to seize the opportunity to do it

02:30:44.969 --> 02:30:46.237
Including when you described Anthropic

02:30:46.237 --> 02:30:48.973
doing coding, it seemed like there was some randomness to it too

02:30:48.973 --> 02:30:50.141
But you have to seize it

02:30:50.174 --> 02:30:52.376
Right, right. But I think when it comes to coding

02:30:52.376 --> 02:30:53.978
it might still involve more

02:30:53.978 --> 02:30:55.646
than the technical stuff on the model side

02:30:55.646 --> 02:30:58.616
a bit more corporate heroism, perhaps

02:30:58.616 --> 02:31:02.186
That is, whether you can bet on it fast enough

02:31:02.186 --> 02:31:04.088
Yeah, Anthropic was indeed very strong in that regard

02:31:04.088 --> 02:31:05.289
But if Anthropic hadn't done it today

02:31:05.289 --> 02:31:06.357
some other company probably would have

02:31:06.390 --> 02:31:08.592
I think so. It's inevitable

02:31:08.592 --> 02:31:10.461
So it's all about emergent capabilities in AI

02:31:11.095 --> 02:31:12.763
It's just about whether you can seize that capability

02:31:12.763 --> 02:31:13.931
Whether it's a company or an individual

02:31:13.998 --> 02:31:14.665
Right, right

02:31:14.665 --> 02:31:19.336
I think before usable language models

02:31:19.336 --> 02:31:21.172
before large-scale language models emerged

02:31:21.539 --> 02:31:23.641
a lot of things were not inevitable

02:31:24.275 --> 02:31:26.143
Like whether someone could invent something

02:31:26.143 --> 02:31:28.546
whether a language model could be trained at scale

02:31:28.946 --> 02:31:30.781
and whether the GPT paradigm

02:31:30.781 --> 02:31:32.083
could be discovered

02:31:32.083 --> 02:31:33.451
There was a lot of uncertainty

02:31:34.351 --> 02:31:37.488
But like you said, for example

02:31:37.488 --> 02:31:39.256
if there had been no Google Brain back then

02:31:39.957 --> 02:31:42.293
Transformer might not have been discovered

02:31:42.293 --> 02:31:43.360
It might have taken many, many years

02:31:43.360 --> 02:31:46.797
before another well-funded organization with talented people discovered it

02:31:46.997 --> 02:31:48.466
That would have been a huge impact

02:31:48.632 --> 02:31:50.334
But after entering that stage

02:31:50.334 --> 02:31:53.671
especially now, the situation has reversed

02:31:53.671 --> 02:31:57.641
Any organization that wants to stop AI progress

02:31:57.975 --> 02:31:58.943
can't do it

02:32:00.878 --> 02:32:02.179
Anthropic has

02:32:02.179 --> 02:32:03.781
Anthropic is very concerned about AI safety

02:32:03.781 --> 02:32:06.083
But does Anthropic have the ability to stop AI development?

02:32:06.083 --> 02:32:07.017
It doesn't

02:32:07.017 --> 02:32:08.319
If you stop developing

02:32:08.319 --> 02:32:08.953
Others will continue

02:32:08.953 --> 02:32:10.321
Your voice will only get smaller

02:32:10.988 --> 02:32:12.490
Right, actually right now it's

02:32:12.490 --> 02:32:14.492
It's more like this kind of situation

02:32:14.492 --> 02:32:16.293
The world is pushing us forward

02:32:16.627 --> 02:32:18.462
Rather than us pushing the world forward

02:32:20.397 --> 02:32:22.500
I feel like in the future it'll be even harder for us to stop AI

02:32:22.500 --> 02:32:25.069
Haha, I think we already can't stop it

02:32:25.803 --> 02:32:26.837
I just think

02:32:28.239 --> 02:32:30.875
Trying to prevent one specific thing from happening with AI

02:32:30.875 --> 02:32:33.210
Probably isn't the right mindset to begin with

02:32:34.044 --> 02:32:37.414
This also relates to what we were just talking about

02:32:37.515 --> 02:32:38.749
Because we were just talking about Anthropic

02:32:38.749 --> 02:32:41.752
One of Anthropic's very important motivations

02:32:41.752 --> 02:32:43.320
Is so-called AI safety

02:32:44.054 --> 02:32:47.124
I think when it comes to AI safety

02:32:47.124 --> 02:32:48.492
The motivation when it was founded

02:32:48.492 --> 02:32:49.360
Right

02:32:49.360 --> 02:32:50.895
What does that have to do with it now

02:32:51.962 --> 02:32:54.732
The relationship now is complicated, meaning

02:32:56.233 --> 02:32:58.102
A natural

02:32:58.102 --> 02:32:59.837
Question people might ask is

02:32:59.837 --> 02:33:01.238
A company focused on AI safety

02:33:01.238 --> 02:33:04.275
Why is it now training frontier models

02:33:04.275 --> 02:33:07.545
Anthropic's explanation is that

02:33:07.545 --> 02:33:09.747
First, I need to have the most cutting-edge model

02:33:09.747 --> 02:33:12.016
Only then do I have a voice to push my AI safety agenda

02:33:12.683 --> 02:33:16.487
So actually, its thinking all along has been

02:33:16.487 --> 02:33:18.355
I want to build the best model in the world

02:33:18.522 --> 02:33:20.224
Everyone will have to listen to me

02:33:20.224 --> 02:33:22.259
To push forward my safety policies

02:33:22.860 --> 02:33:24.828
But from my personal perspective

02:33:24.828 --> 02:33:26.530
I think this idea is very naive

02:33:26.931 --> 02:33:28.165
Looking at this now

02:33:28.165 --> 02:33:30.067
It's not going to happen

02:33:30.067 --> 02:33:30.734
What's more likely to happen is

02:33:30.734 --> 02:33:32.803
Everyone will have great frontier models

02:33:33.103 --> 02:33:35.472
And you won't be able to stop anything from happening

02:33:36.073 --> 02:33:40.644
Maybe for this issue

02:33:40.644 --> 02:33:43.881
What we should focus on and think more about now is

02:33:43.881 --> 02:33:45.482
If you really want to avoid AI

02:33:45.482 --> 02:33:47.651
Bringing about some crisis

02:33:47.651 --> 02:33:51.155
What would be a more self-enforcing approach

02:33:52.456 --> 02:33:53.958
Let me give an example of a self-enforcing mechanism

02:33:53.958 --> 02:33:55.459
Like nuclear weapons, for example

02:33:55.459 --> 02:33:57.861
Nuclear weapons are also something that everyone thinks, hey

02:33:57.861 --> 02:33:59.630
This might have the power to destroy the world

02:33:59.763 --> 02:34:00.931
But with nuclear weapons, in the end

02:34:00.931 --> 02:34:02.266
The way they were ultimately controlled

02:34:02.266 --> 02:34:04.335
Is multi-party control

02:34:04.802 --> 02:34:05.703
In this world

02:34:05.703 --> 02:34:09.139
There are many countries with nuclear weapons

02:34:09.139 --> 02:34:11.242
They all have the ability to destroy each other

02:34:11.675 --> 02:34:14.278
So stability is maintained through this kind of balance of power

02:34:14.612 --> 02:34:17.681
I think if you want to stop AI from doing bad things

02:34:17.681 --> 02:34:18.148
Maybe

02:34:18.148 --> 02:34:21.518
Ultimately, you'll need a similar mechanism to achieve that

02:34:21.518 --> 02:34:22.353
Rather than hoping

02:34:22.353 --> 02:34:23.020
Pinning your hopes on

02:34:23.020 --> 02:34:25.155
One company setting a law to do something

02:34:25.155 --> 02:34:25.689
Mm, right

02:34:25.689 --> 02:34:26.624
And it sets it itself

02:34:26.624 --> 02:34:27.925
It can only govern itself

02:34:28.492 --> 02:34:29.827
Mm, you also just mentioned

02:34:29.827 --> 02:34:31.829
Anthropic has an interpretability team

02:34:31.829 --> 02:34:34.264
Right
How far has their interpretability gotten

02:34:34.531 --> 02:34:37.067
In some relatively simple

02:34:37.067 --> 02:34:41.472
Relatively sparse neural networks

02:34:41.472 --> 02:34:44.241
They can do some interesting research

02:34:44.241 --> 02:34:44.875
For example

02:34:44.875 --> 02:34:48.479
Look at what a certain output

02:34:48.479 --> 02:34:51.482
Or input text or image

02:34:51.482 --> 02:34:54.218
What its internal representation looks like

02:34:54.218 --> 02:34:57.021
And then maybe you invert that representation somehow

02:34:57.021 --> 02:34:59.089
What kind of thing it can output after that

02:34:59.523 --> 02:35:00.958
Doing this kind of research

02:35:03.394 --> 02:35:05.329
You also just mentioned a viewpoint

02:35:05.329 --> 02:35:06.764
That AI is essentially simple

02:35:06.764 --> 02:35:07.931
Can you describe what you mean by this

02:35:07.931 --> 02:35:08.866
This is a conclusion

02:35:09.166 --> 02:35:10.834
Right, I think this is

02:35:10.834 --> 02:35:11.869
This isn't even a conclusion

02:35:11.869 --> 02:35:13.771
It's just my statement（陈述）

02:35:13.904 --> 02:35:15.572
It's my statement

02:35:15.706 --> 02:35:16.907
It could be right or wrong

02:35:16.907 --> 02:35:18.175
Oh, and my explanation for this

02:35:18.175 --> 02:35:19.043
This is your view

02:35:19.076 --> 02:35:20.277
Right, my explanation for this

02:35:20.277 --> 02:35:23.447
My explanation for this statement is

02:35:24.381 --> 02:35:26.617
I think the reason it's essentially simple is

02:35:26.617 --> 02:35:28.385
That you can run experiments

02:35:28.819 --> 02:35:32.823
Like, compared to things that are fundamentally difficult

02:35:32.956 --> 02:35:34.024
Like physics, for example

02:35:34.391 --> 02:35:35.759
The difference is

02:35:35.759 --> 02:35:36.460
With that

02:35:36.460 --> 02:35:38.429
Without experimental data at that energy scale

02:35:38.429 --> 02:35:40.497
You simply can't understand the theory at that energy scale

02:35:41.031 --> 02:35:43.100
But AI isn't bound by this（约束）

02:35:43.100 --> 02:35:45.402
It doesn't matter if you don't understand it

02:35:45.402 --> 02:35:46.370
It can still move forward

02:35:46.370 --> 02:35:47.604
And also right now

02:35:47.604 --> 02:35:48.205
The fact is

02:35:48.205 --> 02:35:50.841
I can do any experiment I can think of

02:35:50.941 --> 02:35:51.642
It's just that possibly

02:35:51.642 --> 02:35:52.543
I need some time

02:35:52.543 --> 02:35:54.645
To scale up the compute

02:35:54.645 --> 02:35:57.047
Or get the infrastructure ready

02:35:57.047 --> 02:35:58.982
But there's no fundamental difficulty

02:35:59.750 --> 02:36:00.551
Right

02:36:01.185 --> 02:36:04.154
So I've always been saying

02:36:04.154 --> 02:36:07.091
I feel AI doesn't give people the sense

02:36:07.358 --> 02:36:08.826
That it's hitting a wall because

02:36:09.593 --> 02:36:12.663
First, you can try many things

02:36:12.830 --> 02:36:13.630
Second

02:36:13.997 --> 02:36:16.400
It's not that everyone has run out of ideas

02:36:16.400 --> 02:36:17.668
With no ideas left to try

02:36:17.668 --> 02:36:19.603
More often it's that there are too many ideas

02:36:19.603 --> 02:36:20.671
Need to try them one by one

02:36:20.671 --> 02:36:21.972
Take time

02:36:21.972 --> 02:36:22.940
Mm-hmm

02:36:24.541 --> 02:36:26.510
Feels like humans are so insignificant

02:36:26.643 --> 02:36:27.945
In front of these experiments

02:36:27.945 --> 02:36:29.113
Yes, so

02:36:29.113 --> 02:36:30.714
I think very soon

02:36:30.714 --> 02:36:33.384
AI might start doing experiments itself

02:36:33.384 --> 02:36:34.718
How soon is very soon

02:36:34.985 --> 02:36:35.786
Within 4 months

02:36:35.919 --> 02:36:37.721
I think in the next 6-12 months

02:36:38.055 --> 02:36:39.289
AI will do experiments itself

02:36:39.289 --> 02:36:40.858
I think of course this statement

02:36:40.858 --> 02:36:41.725
Is not very well-defined

02:36:41.725 --> 02:36:43.394
Sorry I said something very vague

02:36:43.460 --> 02:36:44.762
Like um

02:36:45.863 --> 02:36:47.164
AI improving itself

02:36:47.164 --> 02:36:50.734
Or speeding up its own development process

02:36:50.734 --> 02:36:52.736
This is actually already happening

02:36:53.070 --> 02:36:53.504
Right

02:36:53.504 --> 02:36:55.272
Like we discussed earlier

02:36:55.272 --> 02:36:56.840
It's already helping us

02:36:56.840 --> 02:37:00.744
To achieve some of the things we want

02:37:00.744 --> 02:37:02.379
And speed up our experimental pace

02:37:02.880 --> 02:37:04.882
But I think in the next six to twelve

02:37:04.882 --> 02:37:05.349
Sorry

02:37:05.349 --> 02:37:07.351
What it currently can't do is

02:37:07.351 --> 02:37:09.086
Whether it can

02:37:09.086 --> 02:37:13.323
From start to finish complete an AI research project

02:37:13.524 --> 02:37:15.125
Like not only can it write this code

02:37:15.325 --> 02:37:16.527
It can also run this experiment

02:37:16.660 --> 02:37:17.161
Run this experiment

02:37:17.161 --> 02:37:18.295
Can also see the results

02:37:18.295 --> 02:37:19.329
See the results

02:37:19.329 --> 02:37:20.230
Can also analyze the results

02:37:20.230 --> 02:37:20.898
Analyze the results

02:37:20.898 --> 02:37:21.932
Know where it did wrong

02:37:21.932 --> 02:37:23.500
Then propose new hypotheses

02:37:23.500 --> 02:37:25.402
Design new code

02:37:25.402 --> 02:37:26.403
Run new experiments

02:37:27.171 --> 02:37:29.406
This chain is not yet complete

02:37:30.040 --> 02:37:30.407
But I think

02:37:30.407 --> 02:37:30.974
This chain

02:37:30.974 --> 02:37:33.343
Might be the next thing to gradually become complete

02:37:34.945 --> 02:37:36.413
Based on your various reasons

02:37:36.413 --> 02:37:37.381
At the moment you left

02:37:37.381 --> 02:37:38.982
Decided to leave Anthropic

02:37:39.016 --> 02:37:41.351
What were your expectations for this company's future

02:37:41.518 --> 02:37:43.954
I think when I left

02:37:43.954 --> 02:37:46.156
I was actually quite pessimistic about this company

02:37:47.524 --> 02:37:49.259
But later obviously I was overly pessimistic

02:37:49.259 --> 02:37:50.861
Hehehe why pessimistic

02:37:50.961 --> 02:37:53.330
The reason I was pessimistic at that time was

02:37:53.330 --> 02:37:55.799
I think when I left Anthropic

02:37:55.799 --> 02:37:58.202
Anthropic actually um

02:37:58.769 --> 02:38:01.004
Its main revenue source was API

02:38:01.338 --> 02:38:02.573
Selling tokens

02:38:02.573 --> 02:38:03.707
And

02:38:04.908 --> 02:38:06.543
This is a bad business

02:38:06.543 --> 02:38:07.411
Is a bad business

02:38:07.744 --> 02:38:08.779
Because this business

02:38:08.779 --> 02:38:10.147
Is only a good business for one company

02:38:10.147 --> 02:38:11.181
Which is Google

02:38:11.481 --> 02:38:11.949
Because this

02:38:11.949 --> 02:38:14.985
This business eventually leads to price wars

02:38:15.719 --> 02:38:17.888
Eventually it will be price wars

02:38:17.921 --> 02:38:21.358
In price wars if you don't have the complete chain

02:38:21.425 --> 02:38:24.628
There's not much advantage

02:38:24.628 --> 02:38:28.031
But later Anthropic obviously on the product side

02:38:28.031 --> 02:38:30.033
I think indeed there were many clever ideas

02:38:30.033 --> 02:38:31.001
Did many good things

02:38:31.001 --> 02:38:33.170
Whether it's Claude Code getting better and better

02:38:33.170 --> 02:38:34.304
And Claude Cowork

02:38:34.304 --> 02:38:35.706
And various

02:38:35.706 --> 02:38:37.741
